      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The computational chain removes information in stages aligned with the finite certificate: a nonzero phase converts critical-line zeta values to a real Z function without moving zeros, the Riemann–Siegel representation evaluates that real amplitude with roughly square-root-many terms plus a remainder, and a count-oriented run retains certified sign-change events rather than high-precision zero coordinates.",
