      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1bce18dbdf8f42904d1f999210f5b37318d8b6680a4cee9f802ba449f478948a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The search trajectory is not itself the certificate. In the Jensen-polynomial work, approximate root discovery becomes proof-relevant only through a controlled coefficient-to-root transfer or a justified real-root count; in the trigonometric-polynomial work, annealing proposes a fixed coefficient vector whose admissibility and objective inequalities could serve as the finite upper-bound witness once independently verified.",
