      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3533505d71d986478c94dfaeb2d99637baf49b2c7945b69b33dafd8cdf32f0f3",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Both arguments make a global inequality tractable by partitioning it where different representations are strongest. The Lehmer-pair calculation bounds a finite ordered block from adjacent gaps and controls remote inverse-square mass by zero counts and decay before aggregating component bounds; the zero-free-region calculation splits a whole-line integral at branch changes and around a moving peak, using bounded numerical pieces and analytic tail majorants.",
